Description: Guidelines for creating and managing data models in the Read Leaf project.

Instructions: All core data structures used across the application should be defined as data models, typically in the domain/models/ directory within the relevant feature.

Formats: Utilize freezed for immutability and json_serializable for serialization/deserialization where appropriate.
Persistence: Understand which models are stored locally (Hive) and which are synced/stored in Supabase.

Key Models: Be aware of important existing models like AiCharacter, PublicCharacter, BookMetadata, EpubPageContent, SyncTask, etc..

Behavior: When creating or modifying data models, ensure they are clearly defined, placed in the correct architectural layer, and compatible with the chosen persistence mechanisms.
